			<div class="content" id="post-content-4834738">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article (thinking Euclid Clas)</p>
<p>Genre: Weird Tales/Horror</p>
<p>Page Layout: N/A</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: An antique toybox may not be as harmless as it appears.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: The item in question is an antique toybox, constructed of seasoned, naval grade wood and secured with pig iron fittings. It features an integrated locking mechanism, and is not unlike a seachest in construction.</p>
<p>The toybox contains a variable number of toys appropriate to its size. Toys can vary when a box has been locked and unlocked, but will otherwise remain the same in everyday use.</p>
<p>The locking and unlocking process is somewhat disquieting. In order to be unlocked, the individual physically turning the key must be an individual twelve years of age or younger OR such an individual must be present within the room.</p>
<p>In order to -lock- the box, the individual turning the key must be an adult (aged eighteen years or older). Furthermore, all items that were discovered within the box must have been removed, and then returned.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: Each of the toys might seem harmless enough, but was in fact in its time notoriously unsafe. Where historically appropriate, the item may have been recalled. This might include items such as: a lazertag set with ultra-realistic guns; a batman cape which, when worn, tends to convince the wearer they can glide safely from a height to ground; a bag of marbles that look very much like candy; a set of lawn darts;etc.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: The toybox is incredibly old. Notes will indicate spectrographic analysis showing use at least as far back as the early eighteenth century.</p>

							</div>

								
					
